body:
## Objective
Fix global CSS: add prefers-reduced-motion support, add focus-visible styles, remove decorative patterns (grid background, gradient text), remove Inter font dependency.

## Context
Critique found: no prefers-reduced-motion (WCAG 2.3.3 violation), no focus indicators (WCAG 2.4.7), decorative grid background (slop pattern), gradient text (slop pattern), overused Inter font. User wants music references removed — but that's other builders' files, not yours.

## Files
- `src/styles/global.css` (ONLY this file)

## Action Steps
1. **Add `prefers-reduced-motion` media query** in `@layer base` or after it:
   ```css
   @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
     *, *::before, *::after {
       animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
       animation-iteration-count: 1 !important;
       transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
       scroll-behavior: auto !important;
     }
   }
   ```

2. **Add global focus-visible styles** in `@layer base`:
   ```css
   a:focus-visible,
   button:focus-visible,
   input:focus-visible,
   textarea:focus-visible,
   select:focus-visible,
   [tabindex]:focus-visible {
     outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
     outline-offset: 2px;
     border-radius: 2px;
   }
   ```

3. **Remove the decorative grid background** (`.grid-bg` class). Find the `.grid-bg` definition and DELETE it entirely. It's a codex-grid-background slop pattern.

4. **Remove the gradient text utility** (`.text-gradient` class). Find the `.text-gradient` definition and DELETE it entirely. It's a gradient-text slop pattern. NOTE: AboutCard uses `text-gradient` — another builder is fixing that file to use `text-accent` instead. Just remove the CSS class definition.

5. **Remove Inter from font stack.** In `@theme`, change `--font-sans` to system fonts only:
   ```css
   --font-sans: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
   ```
   Keep `--font-mono` as JetBrains Mono (that provides character).

6. **Also remove `.noise-bg`** if it exists — decorative noise texture is part of the noise overload. If it's used by Layout.astro body class, leave the class definition but make it a no-op (empty rule or comment). Actually, check if `.noise-bg` is defined — if yes, remove the decorative noise pattern from it (keep class as empty hook if needed).

## Constraints
- ONLY edit `src/styles/global.css`
- Preserve all color tokens, easing tokens, font-mono
- Keep scrollbar styles, selection styles, base resets
- Do NOT touch any component files

## Deliverables
- Report exact changes made with line references
- Confirm no other files touched
